  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "In 1947, after something came down near Roswell, New Mexico, an Air Force general named Arthur Exon is said to have held one of the bodies, which he likened to a big insect, when the debris and bodies were brought to Air Materiel Command, the Air Force's equipment and testing command at Wright Field in Ohio. The writer Whitley Strieber tells it, repeating what he says Exon told him. If true, it would mean bodies, not only wreckage, came out of Roswell."
